From: DroidVM bring-up <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] vm: a stale hole list is a lost hint, not a broken map

On this board the client's first exec hits "Illegal action: h1..h3" in
update_holes_on_entry_creation(): the entry exec inserts overlaps no hole in the
map's hole list, although vm_map_enter() had just found the range free in the RB
tree.  The hole list and the tree have drifted apart, and panicking turns that
drift into a dead guest: by then the kernel is fully up (root mounted, 778 MB of
the OS disks read, init exec'ing), so the cost of the panic is the whole boot.

The hole list is an accelerator for first_free, not the authority: the RB tree
holds the entries, vm_map_enter() has already refused a range that is in use, and
neighbouring code already tolerates the same drift ("Found an existing entry ...
instead of potential hole", "Hole hint failed: ...").  A hole that was missed
leaves first_free on an address that may be taken; the next search re-checks the
tree and corrects it.  Nothing is mapped or unmapped by this path.

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_map_store_rb.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_map_store_rb.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_map_store_rb.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_map_store_rb.c
@@ -616,15 +616,23 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	panic("Illegal action: h1: %p, s:0x%llx, e:0x%llx...h2:%p, s:0x%llx, e:0x%llx...h3:0x%p, s:0x%llx, e:0x%llx",
-	    hole_entry->vme_prev,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_prev->vme_start,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_prev->vme_end,
-	    hole_entry,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_start,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_end,
-	    hole_entry->vme_next,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_next->vme_start,
-	    (unsigned long long)hole_entry->vme_next->vme_end);
+	/*
+	 * DroidVM: the hole list is a hint over the RB tree, not the authority.
+	 *
+	 * The entry being placed overlaps no hole even though vm_map_enter() just
+	 * found its range free in the tree: the list has drifted from the entries.
+	 * On this board that happens on the first exec -- the kernel is otherwise
+	 * fully up -- and the panic made the drift fatal.
+	 *
+	 * A missed hole leaves first_free on an address that may be taken;
+	 * vm_map_find_space() re-checks the tree and corrects the hint, the same
+	 * tolerance vm_map_lookup_entry() shows when it finds "an existing entry
+	 * ... instead of potential hole".  Nothing is mapped or unmapped here, so
+	 * skipping the update cannot lose an entry.
+	 */
+	return;
 }
 
 void
